@page "/dashboard"
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>Staff Dashboard</PageTitle>

<h1>Staff Dashboard</h1>

@* Two layers on one page: [Authorize] above already blocked anonymous users from the
   PAGE; <AuthorizeView> here does VISUAL conditional rendering WITHIN it. `context.User`
   is the same ClaimsPrincipal as yesterday's [CascadingParameter]; FindFirst("email")
   reads one specific claim by name. *@
<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <p>Logged in as: <strong>@context.User.FindFirst("email")?.Value</strong></p>
    </Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Orders Today</h5>
                <p class="card-text display-4">42</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Low Stock Items</h5>
                <p class="card-text display-4">7</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Revenue</h5>
                <p class="card-text display-4">$3,450</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@* Admin role check — a silent no-op today, on purpose. The user you sign in as
   (demo@sdev2351.local) holds no roles at all, so the check finds nothing to match and
   renders nothing: no error, no warning, just an empty space where the controls should
   be. That silence has more than one cause — no role, or the app reading the wrong
   claim type — and telling them apart is Day 16's subject. Writing the check before the
   role exists is the enterprise pattern; leave it as is. *@
<AuthorizeView Roles="Admin">
    <Authorized>
        <hr />
        <h2>Admin Controls</h2>
        <p>These controls are only visible to users with the Admin role.</p>
        <button class="btn btn-danger">Reset Daily Stats</button>
        <button class="btn btn-warning">Export Reports</button>
    </Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>
